1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:12,160
Meet Recall, an offline-first AI study companion. It turns your notes into flashcards, a quiz, and a study plan — so you can study on a plane, in a library, or on bad wifi.

2
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:18,212
Quick tasks run on-device with Gemini Nano. Deep tasks go to Gemini Flash in the cloud.

3
00:00:21,110 --> 00:00:32,798
Here are the flashcards, generated on-device. No network round-trip, no data leaves your device — and it works offline. Flip a card to test yourself, and mark anything you're unsure of as still learning.

4
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:47,772
The quiz runs on-device too. Watch: one answer right, one wrong — and the explanation appears either way, so you learn from every mistake. Your score updates live as you go.

5
00:00:54,490 --> 00:01:00,082
Grading a free-text answer needs deeper reasoning, so this one goes to the cloud — Gemini Flash.

6
00:01:03,820 --> 00:01:12,892
Recall builds a seven-day study plan from your notes and your quiz result — a little each day, with the weak spots up first. Scroll through the week and the plan is right there.

7
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:27,880
Stuck on a concept? Just ask. Recall explains it for you — in the cloud, in plain language.

8
00:01:30,610 --> 00:01:36,058
Cards you marked still learning come back here, on a spaced schedule — right when you're about to forget them.

9
00:01:42,070 --> 00:01:49,270
You can force either path with the routing switch. Firebase AI Logic hybrid inference — the same code, on every device.
